---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import styles from "./about.module.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Ann Hagan">
  <p class={styles.eyebrow}>About</p>
  <h1 class={styles.title}>Hi — I'm Ann.</h1>

  <div class={styles.prose}>
    <p>
      I'm an ML/AI engineer who likes to build things that think — agents,
      models, and small systems that turn messy real-world data into decisions
      you can act on.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lately I've been deep in <strong>applied reasoning</strong>: tool-using
      agents, structured outputs, and running capable models locally and on the
      edge instead of leaning on the cloud. I learn by building — most of what's
      here started as "I wonder if…"
    </p>

    <h2>What I work on</h2>
    <p>
      Machine learning and AI, with a bias toward things that ship: agent
      design, local/edge LLMs, machine learning models that answer tough
      questions, and the glue that makes a model actually useful.
    </p>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      My first foray into building applications started with Microsoft
      FrontPage, back when getting something onto the web felt a little like
      magic. I moved through the early rise of WordPress and the evolution of
      modern web development, eventually bringing in the analytical skills I
      developed in another life working with statistics and data. Today, I
      combine that builder mindset with machine learning, artifical
      intelligence, and a healthy curiosity for figuring out how things work—and
      how to make them work better.
    </p>

    <h2>Say hi</h2>
    <p>
      Find me on <a href="https://github.com/anniepuy">GitHub</a>
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ds9MprWUn4g"> YouTube</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
